My summary for my interactions with Ai in this project is as follows:

I used Claude as that Ai was praised by my 341 professor, Prof. Miller, and I can see why.

The LLM provided me with very detailed responses that needed minimal correction. Perhaps this is simply because my prompts were effective or that the LLM has an advanced
knowledge base, or perhaps a combination of the two. Truly for my first time vibe coding, it went quite well. I enjoyed seeing what LLMs are capable of.

My aim in the beginning was to provide the LLM with detailed examples and context so that Claude could better understand what the assignment was and how to complete it
from a practical and aesthetic perspective.

Funny enough, most of my errors were born from my misinterpretation which was quickly caught and remedied.

Additionally, it took me a moment to get the test file properly set up, but I with a few requests, it was easy enough to change.
